CloudBurrow patch 99 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1816). Applies after patch 0097.

A NULL query parameter, positional or named, had no type: a nil arg is
left undeclared (and with one, every positional parameter of the
statement), and an undeclared parameter with no type from its context is
an INT64, so `SELECT @p` with a NULL STRING or DATE was an INT64. An
ARRAY's type came from its first element's Go value and a STRUCT's from
none (a STRING), so an ARRAY<DATE> or ARRAY<NUMERIC> given as text was an
ARRAY<STRING>, and `@p.x` of a STRUCT failed. BigQuery types each as
declared (https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/parameterized-queries).

TypedParameter (patch 0097) is now also a NULL (Null), an ARRAY
(ArrayType, ArrayValues) or a STRUCT (StructTypes, StructValues, in the
fields' order) of its declared type, each element and field a
TypedParameter of its own. Conn.CheckNamedValue keeps a TypedParameter's
declared type with its encoded value (typedArg, a driver.Valuer), the
analyzer declares the parameter, positional or named, with it, and the
statement is run with the encoded value; an INSERT leaves it as it is
rather than reshaping it to the column at its position (VALUES (1, @p,
@a) read an ARRAY<STRUCT> @a as the STRUCT column after id). A BYTES
TypedParameter reads URL-safe and unpadded base64 too, as clients send
it.

typed_null_array_struct_parameter_test.go
(TestTypedNullArrayStructParameters).

